WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.500
I'm back!

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.250
Welcome home!

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:18.180
Shion, the package by the door...

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.680
I forgot!

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.940
I took in Ms. Hannen's package
this morning!

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.650
Ms. Hannen?

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.400
She lives on the second floor.
I have to get it to her!

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.940
But the chicken...

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.700
- Do you want me to take it up?
- What should I do?

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.700
You, Hana?

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.200
Are you sure?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.950
Yeah, no problem.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.170
<i>Even though you were so shy before...</i>

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.670
<i>you've made progress, Hana.</i>

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.040
Shion!

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.470
Tell me what to say after I ring the bell
and hand over the package!

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.880
As detailed as possible!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:57.760
Hana...

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.280
THE PREMIUM TOURNAMENT
ON THE SECOND FLOOR

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:39.910
<i>Yes?</i>

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.780
U-Um, I'm the landlady!

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.790
I've come to deliver a package

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.000
that came when you were out

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.000
this morning!

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.960
<i>Th-That didn't come out strange, did it?</i>

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.680
U-Um...

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.510
Who are you?

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.100
Th-The landlady...

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.350
No, you're not.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.600
The landlady has more up top.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.140
HANDLE WITH CARE

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:09.850
<i>Boom!</i>

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.610
U-Um, but I'm the landlady's—

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.610
The one before the stacked one
was a middle-aged man!

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.450
I see right through your scheme!

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:27.700
<i>H-Help me, Shion!</i>

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.960
So let me give you
a proper introduction this time.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.960
This is Ms. Hannen.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.550
And this is my cousin, Hana.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.170
Hello.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.340
I-It's nice to meet you!

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.680
I'm sorry, Ms. Hannen.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.310
I forgot all about the package.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.480
Not at all! I apologize
for all of the packages that come in.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:53.480
All apologies aside, stay for fried chicken.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.110
Oh, I...

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.110
Ms. Hannen graduated
from high school last year

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.200
and was living here alone
to study for college entrance exams.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:04.660
So right now...

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.500
You're still studying for them, huh?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.040
Yes, because I failed them all!

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.290
This year, too!

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.920
Hot!

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:20.090
<i>I see. Ms. Hannen is here
to study for exams just like I was.</i>

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.800
U-Um, I apologize for before.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.550
I wasn't able to explain myself well.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.810
Oh, well, I apologize
for suddenly yelling at you.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.940
Good, now you've patched things up.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.980
We weren't close enough
to have patched things up.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.950
But now that you've met
and live in the same apartment building,

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.280
you can be friends!

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.040
Go on, shake hands!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.620
Nah, I don't think that's something
the landlady can decide.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.670
Shake hands!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.960
- A-All right. Just this once.
- O-Okay.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.010
<i>Ms. Hannen is shaking?</i>

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:06.850
<i>Hana, too!</i>

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.100
<i>And...</i>

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:10.770
<i>now...</i>

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.060
<i>the shaking has squared!</i>

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.410
U-Um, actually...

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.320
I'm a year behind.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.790
That explains it!

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.790
You're good with umbrellas
because you've been here a year!

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.550
Huh? What?

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.050
You're also good at tying lace sandals.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.430
I-I didn't even realize
I had those abilities!

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.760
Someone with experience like that
has different abilities!

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.890
I think it's cool!

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.270
Viva gap year!

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.140
E-Everyone...

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.060
Then my gap year wasn't a waste.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.730
Thanks, everyone!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:15.500
That was an extremely self-serving dream.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.000
The ball game tournament is in June.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.960
Think about which game you want to enter.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.210
We'll decide on Monday.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.340
Okay!

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.470
Speaking of balls, "tama," right?

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.930
And not to put too fine a point on it,
but that's me, Tama!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.100
I'm prepared to be fawned over
as the tournament's mascot character!

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:35.890
So let's see it!

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.980
- Never mind that. Take your seat.
- Sure.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.820
TAIKAI HANNEN

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.820
Taikai Hannen...

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:54.580
<i>Yes?</i>

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.670
Um, I'm here to give you
a package that came.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.830
<i>Oh, w-wait a second!</i>

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.800
S-Sorry! A big package like that...

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.300
- But it's light—
- It must be heavy!

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.380
Give it to me...

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:12.390
M-Ms. Hannen?

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.390
I'll just leave it here.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.020
Sorry about this.
Making you carry my packages around...

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.770
Even though I'm always at home,

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.400
I've been missing them
because of bad timing.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.570
The landlady holds my packages
for me when that happens.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.910
Um, do you host an event
or something, Ms. Hannen?

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.290
Event?

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.790
It says "Taikai Hannen."
"Taikai" for like a "tournament."

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.620
Oh, it's not read as "Taikai," but "Hiroe."

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:42.330
It's my name.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.960
S-Sorry! That was a terrible mistake!

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.550
Oh, no one can read it.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:52.590
Anyway, despite the size,
this package is really light.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.300
What the heck is in it?

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.480
Scotch tape, huh?

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.600
Yes, that's Scotch tape.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:06.480
Sorry for invading your privacy
on the pretext of delivering a package!

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.940
- I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!
- No, I'm the one who made you bring it!

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.280
That's right! How about some tea?

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:14.620
P-Please don't fuss over me!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.240
H-Huh? I don't have anything.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.620
I thought I had some right here.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.590
<i>Ms. Hannen's apartment...</i>

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.590
<i>It reminds me of my apartment.</i>

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.590
Sorry! Hold on a few minutes!

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.340
I'm gonna order online!

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.890
Y-You don't have to do that for me!

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:36.720
It's okay! I'm a premium member!

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.140
If I order it now, it'll come by this evening!

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.180
Y-You don't have to.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.650
<i>Help, Shion!</i>

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.150
That's not eligible for immediate delivery!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.150
U-Um, if you want a drink,
I can go to the convenience store.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:52.950
Convenience store?

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.450
W-Want to go to the convenience store?

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.370
I-I can't do that!

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.450
Wh-Why not?

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:04.540
I don't have the clothes
to go to the convenience store.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.170
I-It's the convenience store.

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.460
Even the convenience store!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.550
I don't have the clothes to wear
any farther than the garbage cans outside!

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:17.050
Huh? But what about the clothes
you wore for the entrance exams?

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:18.510
I didn't.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.930
I didn't take the exams.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:31.150
Two years ago, when I was
a third-year high school student,

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.450
everything was smooth sailing for me.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.030
I was the president of student council,

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.540
had irreproachable conduct,
and was a high achiever.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:42.910
I was basically a perfect student.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.160
Third-year, Class 2
Seat: 18
Name: Hiroe Hannen

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.160
ABILITY TEST
ENGLISH
ANSWER SHEET

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:47.170
I was told getting into the college
of my choice would be a breeze.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.500
However...

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.880
...on the day of the entrance exam,
there was suddenly heavy snow.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.640
I wasn't discovered for two hours.

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:00.890
After being rescued, I got a terrible cold.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.390
I couldn't take
my backup college's exam,

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:05.730
let alone the one for my first choice.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:06.900
How awful...

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:12.030
<i>Hannen-senpai,
good work on the entrance exam!</i>

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.780
<i>Th-Thanks.</i>

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.410
<i>I'd like to go to the same college as you,</i>

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.530
<i>but I know it's really tough to get in.</i>

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.790
<i>If I do pass the test,
we'll be together again next year!</i>

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.920
<i>Y-Yeah, that's right.</i>

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.540
<i>- Good luck!
- Thanks!</i>

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.170
Staying in town after that got awkward,

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:39.140
so I moved away
and started living alone, but...

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.760
<i>If I do pass the test,
we'll be together again next year!</i>

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.560
Unable to forget that feeling,

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:50.360
I became more and more of a shut-in.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.780
And then, this year's
college entrance exams...

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:58.240
It's so silly. I look like an idiot, right?

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.870
It isn't silly!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.910
I-It isn't silly,

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.540
and you don't look like an idiot!

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.750
Ms. Ichinose...

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.750
I-I...

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.050
I'm a year behind, too.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.100
So you're a year behind in high school, huh?

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.560
It must've been hard on you, Ms. Ichinose.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.390
Oh, no, not really!

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.480
You've had it much rougher, Ms. Hannen!

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.570
No, no, having a gap year
before high school is rough!

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.820
You've had a much tougher time
than me, Ms. Ichinose!

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:40.280
But I am in high school now,
and I've made friends,

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.950
so I'm much better off
than you, Ms. Hannen!

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.080
Much better off...

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.500
I-I'm sorry!

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.250
No, you're right.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.880
When I can't even go
to the convenience store,

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.920
taking college entrance exams
is just a dream.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:12:00.880
U-Um, I'll help you!
Let's do our best together, Ms. Hannen!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.140
Ms. Ichinose...

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.470
The first step should be
going to the convenience store!

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:06.810
Yes, good idea!
My goal is the convenience store!

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.060
That's a low bar...

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:15.320
N-No, you start with small steps
and then keep going.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:21.610
<i>Come to think of it, this is my first time
telling someone about my gap year.</i>

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:23.410
Oh, that's right!

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:25.490
I just remembered!

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:31.620
I have a sweatshirt
with a cute picture on it.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:34.750
What do you think
about wearing this outside?

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:38.760
First off, we need to choose your clothes.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:39.760
You're ignoring me?

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:44.390
I thought you could try
wearing my clothes,

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.260
but they're a little childish.

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:50.020
No, I think it's cute,

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:53.770
but I'm not sure it'd look good on me,
and it's probably a little too small.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.400
Then, what about Shion's clothes?

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:59.280
Well, we are about the same height.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:00.440
<i>Boom!</i>

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:01.820
The top would hang on me.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:03.660
Yeah, it would be too roomy.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.910
Why not order something online?

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.160
I didn't think of that!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:09.540
SUMMER DRESS SALE!

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.420
<i>She even bought Scotch tape online?</i>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.050
Ms. Hannen,
you don't need to look at sweats.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:24.510
I couldn't help it!

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.680
Sleeveless Shirt Dress

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:28.810
No good.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:31.020
I have no idea what to buy!

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:35.440
I guess we should go to a store
and look at the real thing.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:37.610
Sorry.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:39.480
No, go ahead.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.900
<i>Hello-hello, it's Tamate!</i>

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.320
Tama, what's up?

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:50.040
<i>Are we supposed to turn in
that math worksheet on Monday?</i>

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.290
<i>No, Wednesday.</i>

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.330
That's a relief!

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:57.460
I forgot mine at school!

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.670
<i>Oh, really?</i>

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.970
<i>Actually, Tama,
I'd like to ask you for advice.</i>

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:07.800
<i>I see!</i>

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:11.600
<i>When it comes to that kind of thing,
talking to Eiko is your best bet!</i>

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:15.390
Good idea! Eiko seems to be
in the know about clothes.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.440
<i>I'll go ahead and send her an e-mail!</i>

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.570
Thank you, Tama!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:21.690
<i>Talk to you later!</i>

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.320
Yep! Bye-bye!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.240
EIKO TOKURA

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:26.910
Eiko?

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.200
Hello?

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.290
<i>Hana? I just got an e-mail
from Tama, but it says,</i>

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:35.290
<i>"It seems you're free
to do whatever you please</i>

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:37.830
<i>with Hana's acquaintance,
a 20-year-old woman, he-he."</i>

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.330
<i>What does that mean?</i>

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.340
Tama...

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.210
Coming!

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.300
The see-no-evil monkey is here!

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.100
The speak-no-evil monkey is here!

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:53.010
And I'm the no-fashion-faux-pas monkey!

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.850
I'm here to dress you up...

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:56.730
in fashionable attire!

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:03.360
Um, Hana, Tamate is the one
who wanted to do this.

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.280
Eiko and I aren't to blame.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:07.610
You two are both turncoats!

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:09.740
Hiroe?

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.460
Nice to meet you. I'm Eiko Tokura.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.130
M-Ms. Tokura...

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.460
It's Eiko.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.050
M-Ms. To—

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.840
E-i-ko.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:27.970
E-E-Eiko...

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.470
There, you did it!

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.140
Wow, Eiko is insistent.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:35.810
She sure is.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.230
Did you two go somewhere today?

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.820
Oh, these are my lounging-around clothes.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:46.900
Me, too.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:51.200
I wanted to change, but Eiko rushed me.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:55.740
It's a waste to only wear
an adorable outfit like that at home!

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.160
Aw, you look like an angel!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.420
This is my parents' hobby.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.920
Your parents have great taste!

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.170
Good job!

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:07.840
I guess there are all kinds
of at-home clothes.

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.680
Not counting that.

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:15.180
All right...

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:19.430
I think these would look good on Hiroe.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.190
Just change clothes?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.190
Or do everything
with hair and makeup, too?

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.030
Which pattern should we do?

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.150
Um...

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.030
Everything!

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:41.870
<i>That was the moment
my curiosity exceeded my consideration.</i>

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.880
That was so much fun!

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:48.050
What a blast! Thank you, Hana!

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:49.800
Th-Thank you.

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.300
<i>They did what they pleased
with a 20-year-old woman.</i>

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:56.550
So let's take a look.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:59.310
I give you Hiroe!

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:12.700
Well?

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.820
- Who's that?
- Who's that?

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:16.070
D-Do I look that different?

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:20.040
You're a true technician, Eiko.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.660
Not at all.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:26.080
Maybe you're also a different person
when you take your makeup off, Eiko?

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.040
No, I'm not wearing any makeup.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:30.210
You're terrible, Tama.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:32.880
Th-This is me?

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:36.890
So now that you're dressed up,
where are you going? A class reunion?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.720
C-Convenience store.

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:42.140
Convenience store?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.650
I see. So that's what it is.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.480
If that's the case,
then how about this look instead?

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.700
Good! That's very good, Ms. Hannen!

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:56.160
Really?

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:57.370
It's pretty good.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:01.200
<i>A young woman I don't know
is back to being Ms. Hannen!</i>

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.080
Welcome home, Ms. Hannen!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.540
I-I'm back.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.170
Well, you're ready,

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.670
so go shopping and buy yourself
some clothes and shoes.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.630
Oh, I can't! I'm not prepared for that!

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.600
After all, you don't even have the clothes
to go to a convenience store.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.680
I-I'll just borrow your clothes today.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.560
Yes, but the issue won't go away
by the end of the day.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:26.810
I-I was thinking that today's goal
is going to the convenience store.

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:29.020
Kamu?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.570
Is that really enough?

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:36.030
Is it really enough
just to go to the convenience store?

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.200
Oh, that's true.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:48.250
Here I am, trying again to run away
from the problem in front of me.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:50.670
Ms. Hannen...

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.800
I never thought a little girl like this
would point that out to me.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:58.640
M-Ms. Hannen...

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.800
Kamuri is mad.

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:13.480
Whew, my HP sure has dropped!

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:16.650
The clerks at clothing stores
sure are persistent.

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:19.410
True.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:22.030
Here's a list of matching outfits.

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:23.660
Th-Thank you.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:27.040
I'm not good at that kind of stuff,
so it's a big help.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.580
If you have any questions,
don't hesitate to contact me.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.130
I can come over anytime!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.960
Oh, I don't...

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:34.130
And also...

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.130
Eiko is pushier than any sales clerk.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.130
You're right about that.

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:59.860
I'm glad you were able to find
some really nice clothes today.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:04.370
Thank you, Ms. Ichinose.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:08.370
If you and your friends
hadn't dragged me out of the apartment,

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.620
I doubt I would've ever left it.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:13.880
I'm really grateful.

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:16.340
Ms. Hannen...

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.260
M-Ms. Ichinose,

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:24.390
have you told your friends
about your gap year?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.390
Um, actually...

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:27.850
No.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:29.140
I see.

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:30.600
Yeah, makes sense.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:37.280
Sometimes I think that telling them
wouldn't change anything, but...

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:40.280
But you're scared
that it would change things.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.160
So you can't tell them.

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:43.530
I get it.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.740
You understand?

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:49.790
I do! I totally understand!

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:53.920
Th-This may be the first time
someone's understood it!

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:57.800
And this is the first time
I've felt such an affinity for someone!

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:01.050
U-Um, is it okay if I call you Hiroe?

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:03.430
Of course! Call me that all the time!

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.550
And I want to call you Hana!

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:06.470
Hiroe!

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:07.390
Hana!

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:08.220
Hiroe!

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:09.310
Hana!

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:20.940
But even so...

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:24.030
I do want to tell them the truth sometime.

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.070
Yeah.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:29.370
But you can do it in your own good time.

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:39.420
But if I don't stress about it,
then I can't actually imagine doing it.

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:40.590
I understand.

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.760
I so understand, Hana.

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.270
Oh!

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.440
Good morning, Ms. Hannen.

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:02.740
Oh, hi! Good morning!

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:04.570
Going out?

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:08.160
Just to the convenience store!
